<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade 3 Unit5 Lesson1 Name the Parts"><h2>Unit fractions are equal-area pieces of a whole</h2><p>Original warm-up A rectangle diagonal equal halves, B shaded equal half, C circle equal halves, D rectangle unequal parts. A shape split into two UNEQUAL areas does not show halves.</p><h2>Original 2021 Card Sort A–L: 12 distinct source-labelled mathematical figures</h2><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Card</th><th>Shape</th><th>Parts</th><th>Equal-area?</th><th>Source geometry</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>A</th><td>circle</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td><td>vertical diameter, equal semicircles</td></tr><tr><th>B</th><td>square</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td><td>both perpendicular centered segments, four equal quarters</td></tr><tr><th>C</th><td>rectangle</td><td>2</td><td>No</td><td>off-center vertical cut creates two unequal regions</td></tr><tr><th>D</th><td>circle</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td><td>cross-shaped two perpendicular centered diameters, quarters</td></tr><tr><th>E</th><td>square</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td><td>centered horizontal cut, two equal halves</td></tr><tr><th>F</th><td>rectangle</td><td>2</td><td>Yes</td><td>centered vertical cut, two equal halves</td></tr><tr><th>G</th><td>rectangle</td><td>3</td><td>Yes</td><td>two evenly spaced horizontal cuts, equal thirds</td></tr><tr><th>H</th><td>circle</td><td>3</td><td>No</td><td>two oblique parallel-style cuts, three unequal areas</td></tr><tr><th>I</th><td>square</td><td>2</td><td>No</td><td>off-corner diagonal partial cut forms a small triangle and large remainder</td></tr><tr><th>J</th><td>circle</td><td>3</td><td>Yes</td><td>three equal central sectors, thirds</td></tr><tr><th>K</th><td>rectangle</td><td>3</td><td>Yes</td><td>two evenly spaced vertical cuts, thirds</td></tr><tr><th>L</th><td>rectangle</td><td>4</td><td>Yes</td><td>three evenly spaced vertical cuts, fourths</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The ORIGINAL instructions allow any TWO justified categories chosen by students. One teacher-highlighted category: equal A,B,D,E,F,G,J,K,L; unequal C,H,I. This table transcribes mathematical relations, not original publisher image artwork.</p><h2>Fold and Name — independent diagrams of unit fractions</h2><div style="margin:10px 0"><strong>1/2: 2 equal strips</strong><div role="img" aria-label="One whole rectangle divided into 2 equal-area vertical parts" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,100px);width:max-content"><span style="display:block;width:100px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:#d9edf7" aria-label="Part 1"></span><span style="display:block;width:100px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 2"></span></div></div><div style="margin:10px 0"><strong>1/3: 3 equal strips</strong><div role="img" aria-label="One whole rectangle divided into 3 equal-area vertical parts" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,66px);width:max-content"><span style="display:block;width:66px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:#d9edf7" aria-label="Part 1"></span><span style="display:block;width:66px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 2"></span><span style="display:block;width:66px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 3"></span></div></div><div style="margin:10px 0"><strong>1/4: 4 equal strips</strong><div role="img" aria-label="One whole rectangle divided into 4 equal-area vertical parts" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,50px);width:max-content"><span style="display:block;width:50px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:#d9edf7" aria-label="Part 1"></span><span style="display:block;width:50px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 2"></span><span style="display:block;width:50px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 3"></span><span style="display:block;width:50px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 4"></span></div></div><div style="margin:10px 0"><strong>1/6: 6 equal strips</strong><div role="img" aria-label="One whole rectangle divided into 6 equal-area vertical parts" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(6,33px);width:max-content"><span style="display:block;width:33px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:#d9edf7" aria-label="Part 1"></span><span style="display:block;width:33px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 2"></span><span style="display:block;width:33px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 3"></span><span style="display:block;width:33px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 4"></span><span style="display:block;width:33px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 5"></span><span style="display:block;width:33px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 6"></span></div></div><div style="margin:10px 0"><strong>1/8: 8 equal strips</strong><div role="img" aria-label="One whole rectangle divided into 8 equal-area vertical parts" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(8,25px);width:max-content"><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:#d9edf7" aria-label="Part 1"></span><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 2"></span><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 3"></span><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 4"></span><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 5"></span><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 6"></span><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 7"></span><span style="display:block;width:25px;height:48px;border:1px solid #567;background:white" aria-label="Part 8"></span></div></div><p>Source pupils fold FOUR physical rectangles into3,6,4,8 equal parts, then label fractions. The numerical bottom denominator names count of equal parts, top1 names one chosen part. Publisher blackline page and gated source Cool-down not certified. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-5/lesson-1/lesson.html">Original 2021 teacher lesson</a></p></section>
